.el .ds Aq '
.TH FATHOM_DIFFTOOL 1  "fathom 0.1.0-alpha.1" 
.SH NAME
fathom\-difftool \- Show one file\*(Aqs two sides in your own difftool — difftastic, meld, kdiff3, `vim \-d` (`e5.8`)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfathom difftool\fR [\fB\-\-root\fR] [\fB\-\-path\fR] [\fB\-\-tool\fR] [\fB\-\-print\fR] [\fB\-\-list\fR] [\fB\-\-keep\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIEPISODE\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show one file\*(Aqs two sides in your own difftool — difftastic, meld, kdiff3, `vim \-d` (`e5.8`)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fI<ROOT>\fR [default: .]
The repository to read
.TP
\fB\-\-path\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Which of the episode\*(Aqs files to show, by path or by a unique suffix of it
.TP
\fB\-\-tool\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Which difftool to use, overriding `$FATHOM_DIFFTOOL` and your user config.

A name from the table (`difftastic`, `meld`, `kdiff3`, `nvim`, `vim`, `vscode`, …) or any program on `PATH`, which gets the two files as its last two arguments.
.TP
\fB\-\-print\fR
Print the command and the reason for it, and run nothing. The two files stay on disk
.TP
\fB\-\-list\fR
List every file the episode touched with the line each would jump to, and show nothing
.TP
\fB\-\-keep\fR
Leave the two staged files behind and say where they are
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the decision as JSON on stdout, and nothing else there
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
[\fIEPISODE\fR]
The episode whose file to show: the same handle grammar as every other verb. With no argument, `HEAD`
